[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Inline formatting
[/meta]

h1. Inline Formatting

Tests for Section 5 of the specification. Inputs start with a word where needed, so that no line begins with a list marker.

h2. Elements

h3. Bold {#inline-bold}
[code om]
Some *bold* text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <strong>bold</strong> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Italic {#inline-italic}
[code om]
Some _italic_ text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <em>italic</em> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Underline {#inline-underline}
[code om]
Some __underlined__ text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <u>underlined</u> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Deletion {#inline-deleted}
[code om]
Some -deleted- text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <del>deleted</del> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Insertion {#inline-inserted}
[code om]
Some +inserted+ text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <ins>inserted</ins> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Subscript {#inline-subscript}
[code om]
Some ~subscript~ text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <sub>subscript</sub> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Superscript {#inline-superscript}
[code om]
Some ^superscript^ text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <sup>superscript</sup> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Keyboard {#inline-kbd}
[code om]
Press =Enter= to continue
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to continue</p>
[/code]

h3. Highlight {#inline-highlight}
[code om]
Some ==highlighted== text
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some <mark>highlighted</mark> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Code {#inline-code}
[code om]
Call `print()` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Call <code>print()</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Several words inside markers {#inline-several-words}
[code om]
This is *quite important* indeed
[/code]
[code html]
<p>This is <strong>quite important</strong> indeed</p>
[/code]

h3. Whole paragraph formatted {#inline-whole-paragraph}
[code om]
_Everything here_
[/code]
[code html]
<p><em>Everything here</em></p>
[/code]

h3. Bold at line start is not a list item {#inline-bold-line-start}
A list marker needs a following space, so this line is a paragraph.
[code om]
*Bold* start
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>Bold</strong> start</p>
[/code]

h3. Deletion at line start is not a list item {#inline-deleted-line-start}
[code om]
-Old- text
[/code]
[code html]
<p><del>Old</del> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Two spans on one line {#inline-two-spans}
[code om]
Both *a* and *b* here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Both <strong>a</strong> and <strong>b</strong> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Adjacent spans of different kinds {#inline-adjacent-spans}
[code om]
Then *bold*_italic_ together
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Then <strong>bold</strong><em>italic</em> together</p>
[/code]

h3. Unpaired marker is literal {#inline-unpaired}
[code om]
An *unclosed marker here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>An *unclosed marker here</p>
[/code]

h2. Nesting

h3. Bold italic {#inline-nesting-bold-italic}
[code om]
*_bold italic_*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong><em>bold italic</em></strong></p>
[/code]

h3. Bold inside italic {#inline-nesting-bold-in-italic}
[code om]
Text _italic with *bold* inside_ end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <em>italic with <strong>bold</strong> inside</em> end</p>
[/code]

h3. Three levels {#inline-nesting-three-levels}
[code om]
Press *_=Esc=_* now
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Press <strong><em><kbd>Esc</kbd></em></strong> now</p>
[/code]

h3. Keyboard inside highlight {#inline-nesting-kbd-in-highlight}
[code om]
Text ==Press =Enter= now== end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <mark>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> now</mark> end</p>
[/code]

h3. Italic inside underline {#inline-nesting-italic-in-underline}
[code om]
Text __under _and italic_ line__ end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <u>under <em>and italic</em> line</u> end</p>
[/code]

h3. An element cannot nest inside itself {#inline-nesting-same-element}
The second `*` would open a span of a kind that is already open, so it is literal. The third `*` closes the first.
[code om]
*outer *inner* outer*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>outer *inner</strong> outer*</p>
[/code]

h2. Strict Pairing

h3. Overlapping markers are literal {#inline-overlap}
[code om]
*_bad overlap*_
[/code]
[code html]
<p>*_bad overlap*_</p>
[/code]

h3. Overlap makes every opener above it literal {#inline-overlap-openers-above}
[code om]
Text *a _b =c* d_ e= end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *a _b =c* d_ e= end</p>
[/code]

h3. Overlap does not affect spans already closed {#inline-overlap-closed-spans}
[code om]
Text _x_ *a _b* c
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <em>x</em> *a _b* c</p>
[/code]

h3. An unclosed inner opener makes the outer pair overlap {#inline-overlap-unclosed-inner}
[code om]
Text *a _b c* end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *a _b c* end</p>
[/code]

h3. An unclosed outer opener is literal at the end of the line {#inline-unclosed-outer}
[code om]
Text *a _b_ c
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *a <em>b</em> c</p>
[/code]

h3. Markers pair only within one line {#inline-pairing-one-line}
[code om]
*bold
text* here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>*bold<br>
text* here</p>
[/code]

h2. Marker Boundaries

h3. Spaces inside both markers {#inline-boundary-spaces-inside}
[code om]
Text * not bold * here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text * not bold * here</p>
[/code]

h3. Space before the closing marker {#inline-boundary-space-before-closer}
[code om]
Text *also not bold * here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *also not bold * here</p>
[/code]

h3. Hyphens inside words {#inline-boundary-hyphenated}
[code om]
It is well-known and self-evident
[/code]
[code html]
<p>It is well-known and self-evident</p>
[/code]

h3. Underscores inside words {#inline-boundary-snake-case}
[code om]
Use snake_case_name here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Use snake_case_name here</p>
[/code]

h3. Equals signs between letters {#inline-boundary-equals}
[code om]
Set a=b and c=d
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Set a=b and c=d</p>
[/code]

h3. Asterisks between digits {#inline-boundary-digits}
[code om]
Compute 2*3*4 now
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Compute 2*3*4 now</p>
[/code]

h3. Plus signs inside a keyboard span {#inline-boundary-ctrl-alt-del}
[code om]
=Ctrl+Alt+Del=
[/code]
[code html]
<p><kbd>Ctrl+Alt+Del</kbd></p>
[/code]

h3. Closing marker followed by a letter {#inline-boundary-closer-before-letter}
[code om]
Text *bold*ly here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *bold*ly here</p>
[/code]

h3. Opening marker preceded by a letter {#inline-boundary-opener-after-letter}
[code om]
Text un*believ*able here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text un*believ*able here</p>
[/code]

h3. Equals with spaces around {#inline-boundary-spaced-equals}
[code om]
Test if a == b then
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Test if a == b then</p>
[/code]

h3. Markers next to punctuation {#inline-boundary-punctuation}
Punctuation is neither a letter nor a digit nor whitespace.
[code om]
Text (*bold*), "_italic_" and -gone-.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text (<strong>bold</strong>), "<em>italic</em>" and <del>gone</del>.</p>
[/code]

h3. Cyrillic text is formatted {#inline-boundary-cyrillic}
[code om]
Це *жирний* текст
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Це <strong>жирний</strong> текст</p>
[/code]

h3. Cyrillic letters count as letters {#inline-boundary-cyrillic-intraword}
[code om]
Слово_з_підкресленням тут
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Слово_з_підкресленням тут</p>
[/code]

h3. Combining marks count as letters {#inline-boundary-combining-mark}
The character before the first `*` is a combining acute accent (U+0301), General Category M.
[code om]
Наголос: сло́*во* тут
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Наголос: сло́*во* тут</p>
[/code]

h3. An escaped non-breaking space is whitespace {#inline-boundary-escaped-nbsp}
[code om]
Text *\ bold* here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *&nbsp;bold* here</p>
[/code]

h3. A typed non-breaking space is whitespace {#inline-boundary-typed-nbsp}
The input is `Text *`, U+00A0, `bold* here`.
[code hex]
54 65 78 74 20 2A C2 A0 62 6F 6C 64 2A 20 68 65 72 65
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *&nbsp;bold* here</p>
[/code]

h3. An escaped character counts as itself {#inline-boundary-escaped-backslash}
The `*` follows a backslash, which is not a letter, so it opens.
[code om]
Text \\*bold* here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text \<strong>bold</strong> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped markers are not markers {#inline-boundary-escaped-markers}
[code om]
Text \*not bold\* here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *not bold* here</p>
[/code]

h3. An escaped closer leaves the span unclosed {#inline-boundary-escaped-closer}
[code om]
Text *bold\* here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text *bold* here</p>
[/code]

h3. CJK characters count as letters {#inline-boundary-cjk}
Text without spaces between words cannot be formatted mid-sentence. This is a known limitation of the boundary rule.
[code om]
中文*粗体*中文
[/code]
[code html]
<p>中文*粗体*中文</p>
[/code]

h2. Subscript and Superscript Exemption

h3. Chemistry and physics {#inline-exemption-spec-example}
[code om]
H~2~O and E=mc^2^
[/code]
[code html]
<p>H<sub>2</sub>O and E=mc<sup>2</sup></p>
[/code]

h3. Superscript after a number {#inline-exemption-ordinal}
[code om]
The 10^th^ floor
[/code]
[code html]
<p>The 10<sup>th</sup> floor</p>
[/code]

h3. Whitespace conditions still apply {#inline-exemption-whitespace}
[code om]
Then E=mc^ 2^ fails
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Then E=mc^ 2^ fails</p>
[/code]

h3. Approximate tildes stay literal {#inline-exemption-approximate}
A tilde preceded by a space cannot close a span.
[code om]
It takes ~5 to ~10 minutes
[/code]
[code html]
<p>It takes ~5 to ~10 minutes</p>
[/code]

h3. Closing is tried before opening {#inline-exemption-close-first}
[code om]
Formula H~2~SO~4~ here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Formula H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Consecutive superscripts {#inline-exemption-consecutive}
[code om]
Expand x^2^y^3^ here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Expand x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>3</sup> here</p>
[/code]

h2. Marker Runs

h3. Double underscore is underline, not double italic {#inline-double-underline}
[code om]
Text __word__ here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <u>word</u> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Double underscore around an identifier {#inline-double-dunder}
Underline wins; use a code span for identifiers like this.
[code om]
Call __init__ first
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Call <u>init</u> first</p>
[/code]

h3. Double equals is highlight, not double keyboard {#inline-double-highlight}
[code om]
Text ==word== here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <mark>word</mark> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Double asterisks are literal {#inline-run-double-asterisk}
Bold in OireMark is a single `*`.
[code om]
**bold** here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>**bold** here</p>
[/code]

h3. Triple underscores are literal {#inline-run-triple-underscore}
[code om]
Text ___x___ here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text ___x___ here</p>
[/code]

h3. Triple equals are literal {#inline-run-triple-equals}
[code om]
Text ===x=== here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text ===x=== here</p>
[/code]

h3. Double plus signs are literal {#inline-run-double-plus}
[code om]
Text ++x++ here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text ++x++ here</p>
[/code]

h3. Empty content is literal {#inline-run-empty}
[code om]
Text (--) and (**) and (==) here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text (--) and (**) and (==) here</p>
[/code]

h2. Code Spans

h3. Backslashes are ordinary characters {#inline-code-backslashes}
[code om]
Path `C:\Users\` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Path <code>C:\Users\</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. A lone backslash in a span {#inline-code-lone-backslash}
[code om]
Backslash `\` alone
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Backslash <code>\</code> alone</p>
[/code]

h3. No escapes inside {#inline-code-no-escapes}
[code om]
Literal `\*` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Literal <code>\*</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. No formatting inside {#inline-code-no-formatting}
[code om]
Literal `*not bold* and _not italic_` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Literal <code>*not bold* and _not italic_</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Backtick inside a double-backtick span {#inline-code-double-run}
[code om]
Text `` a`b `` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <code>a`b</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Span beginning and ending with a backtick {#inline-code-quoted}
[code om]
Text `` `quoted` `` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <code>`quoted`</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Double run without padding spaces {#inline-code-double-run-unpadded}
[code om]
Text ``a`b`` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <code>a`b</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Only one space is stripped from each side {#inline-code-strip-one-space}
[code om]
Text ``  a`b  `` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <code> a`b </code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Space on one side only is kept {#inline-code-space-one-side}
[code om]
Text ` a` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <code> a</code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Content made only of spaces is kept {#inline-code-only-spaces}
[code om]
Text `  ` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <code>  </code> here</p>
[/code]

h3. Unclosed span is literal {#inline-code-unclosed}
[code om]
An `unclosed span here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>An `unclosed span here</p>
[/code]

h3. Runs of different length do not match {#inline-code-run-mismatch}
[code om]
Text `a`` here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text `a`` here</p>
[/code]

h3. A span cannot cross a line break {#inline-code-same-line}
[code om]
Start `open
close` end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Start `open<br>
close` end</p>
[/code]

h3. Spans may appear inside words {#inline-code-inside-word}
[code om]
Text foo`bar`baz here
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text foo<code>bar</code>baz here</p>
[/code]

h3. An escaped backtick cannot open a span {#inline-code-escaped-backtick}
The escaped backtick is literal. The second backtick has no closing run on the line, so it is literal too.
[code om]
Text a \`b` c
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text a `b` c</p>
[/code]

h2. Precedence

h3. A marker inside a code span does not close bold {#inline-precedence-code-over-bold}
[code om]
*bold `code*` here*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>bold <code>code*</code> here</strong></p>
[/code]

h3. A marker inside a code span does not close italic {#inline-precedence-code-over-italic}
[code om]
Text _a `_` b_ end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <em>a <code>_</code> b</em> end</p>
[/code]

h3. Code span inside bold {#inline-precedence-code-in-bold}
[code om]
Text *`code`* end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <strong><code>code</code></strong> end</p>
[/code]

h2. Markers and Links

h3. A link can end a formatted span {#inline-link-ends-span}
A trailing marker character is removed from the end of a URL.
[code om]
*see [docs]:https://example.com*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>see <a href="https://example.com">docs</a></strong></p>
[/code]

h3. A marker inside link text never pairs with one outside {#inline-link-text-own-pairing}
The `*` inside the link text is literal. The outer pair makes bold, because a link next to a marker counts as punctuation.
[code om]
*[a*]:https://example.com b*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong><a href="https://example.com">a*</a> b</strong></p>
[/code]

h3. A marker inside a language span never pairs with one outside {#inline-lang-own-pairing}
[code om]
Text *a [lang fr]b* c[/lang] d*
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <strong>a <span lang="fr">b* c</span> d</strong></p>
[/code]

h3. Markers inside a URL are literal {#inline-link-url-literal}
Only the final `_` is removed from the URL; the one inside it stays.
[code om]
Text _read [it]:https://example.com/a_b_ end
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text <em>read <a href="https://example.com/a_b">it</a></em> end</p>
[/code]
